Description: Provides tools to formalize verbal hypotheses about proportions
    as order-constrained models, compute their H-representation (half-space)
    and V-representation (extreme cases), and derive parsimony (the volume of
    a model) and the largest possible Bayes factor against the unconstrained
    model. Also builds intersections and mixtures of models, three kinds of
    replication models, and compares sets of models. Reproduces the examples
    of Jekel, Regenwetter, Chen, and Line (in preparation), "Wait, what are
    you saying, exactly?", and of its online supplement.
